{"parentUuid":"83a831f9-b4c9-462e-8a9d-e6c77bdb50b8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfxbMPNzqgWRZAEuLgsZN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Written for: hackathon judges and developers reading #neatHack on X.\n\n## About the Entire graph\nNo, version 3 did not demo it. The narration mentioned the code graph, but the screen only showed Entire's website. I have fixed that: **use version 4**, which is selected in Finder now.\n\n```\n/Users/Apple/Desktop/Veritas-demo-v4.mp4\n```\n\nVersion 4 adds two screens to Part 2, right after Entire is introduced:\n- A terminal showing real `entire graph impact` output from the Veritas repository, answering \"what breaks if this one function changes?\"\n- The cursor moves through the callers, the dependencies, and the files that change together, while the narration explains each.\n\nThe output on screen is real, run a few minutes ago, and saved in the evidence folder. Everything else is the same as version 3. It runs 2 minutes 57 seconds. I checked the new frame; I cannot hear or watch it play.\n\n## The post\nThis follows the form's template: it opens with \"Our #neatHack submission\", tells the story, and ends with all three tags.\n\n```\nOur #neatHack submission\n\nVeritas is an AI agent that proves which npm upgrades will break your code, then fixes them.\n\nDependency alerts tell you a package is out of date. They don't tell you if upgrading breaks anything, so teams ignore them. Veritas reads the release notes, finds where your code is affected, runs your own tests before and after, writes the smallest fix, and opens a pull request only after you approve.\n\nOn our benchmark: 9/9 verdicts correct, 7/7 fixes passed a hidden test, 0 false alarms, about 9 cents per repository.\n\nWhat surprised me most was neatlogs. While I was testing, my agent started failing. neatlogs raised the incident on its own, investigated six traces, found the root cause (the model was answering without editing any code) and recommended the fix. I sent it to my coding agent straight from the incident, shipped it, and marked it resolved. Earlier it even opened a pull request itself that took refused edits from 12 to 0.\n\nEntire's code graph is how the agent finds where a package is used, and every commit carries an Entire checkpoint.\n\ncfo.ai showed my first pricing lost money on every customer. The revised plan stays funded for 12 months.\n\nLive: https://veritas.milliebanned.xyz\nCode: https://github.com/Milliebanned/Veritas\n\nBuilt with @arithecfo @EntireHQ @neatlogs\n```\n\n## How to post it\n1. On the form, click **Quote on X**. It opens X with the official post already attached and the template text filled in.\n2. Select all the text in the box, delete it, and paste the post above.\n3. Click the image icon and attach the video. In the file window press **Cmd + Shift + G**, paste the path below, press Enter, then click **Open**:\n   ```\n   /Users/Apple/Desktop/Veritas-demo-v4.mp4\n   ```\n4. Wait until the video finishes uploading, then click **Post**. Keep it public and do not remove the quoted post.\n5. Copy the link to your post and go back to the form for steps 2 and 3.\n\nSend me a screenshot of the form's next step if it asks for anything you are unsure about, and send me the post link afterwards so I can log it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":200,"cache_read_input_tokens":451089,"output_tokens":1076,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":200,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1076,"cache_read_input_tokens":451089,"cache_creation_input_tokens":200,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral